ooh, fun! depth first search. ok, so we're going to traverse the graph, visit each node, and mark it as visited. we'll keep track of the path and backtrack when we hit a dead end. we use a stack to manage our path. mrrp, actually, let me show you some pseudocode >~<
```python
function dfs(node):
    if node is visited:
        return
    visit(node)
    for neighbor in node.neighbors:
        dfs(neighbor)
```

